  "body": "## Description\n\nFixes #6628 \u2014 MCP OAuth flows were unusable behind a reverse proxy.\n\n### Problem 1: Login redirect used the internal container origin\n\nThe `/api/mcp/oauth/authorize` route redirect to `/auth/login` was built from `url.origin`, which resolves to the internal container hostname (`<container-id>:3000`) when Homarr runs in Docker behind a proxy.\n\nMCP OAuth URLs now use the configured public `BASE_URL` when present. Deployments without `BASE_URL` retain the existing `x-forwarded-proto` / `x-forwarded-host` / `host` fallback.\n\n### Problem 2: `/.well-known/oauth-*` discovery endpoints returned 404\n\nNext.js's App Router does not route folders with a dot prefix, so the OAuth authorization-server and protected-resource metadata at `/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server` and `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` were unreachable. The folders were moved to `well-known/` and rewrites keep the public URLs working:\n\n- `/.well-known/:path*` for RFC 8414 and RFC 9728 root and path-inserted discovery\n- `/api/mcp/:transport/.well-known/:path*` for clients using endpoint-appended discovery\n\nBoth forms preserve the transport-specific resource or issuer identifier. The MCP `WWW-Authenticate` challenge advertises the matching RFC 9728 path-inserted metadata URL.\n\nNo new environment variable or public URL was added. The existing `BASE_URL` behavior is now documented explicitly for OAuth metadata and redirects.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Focused OAuth metadata tests pass\n- [x] Next.js lint passes with no errors\n- [x] Next.js typecheck passes\n- [x] Docs lint passes with no errors\n- [x] No new dependencies\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added OAuth metadata discovery through standardized `.well-known` endpoints.\n  * Added CORS support for metadata requests, including preflight handling.\n  * Improved MCP authentication responses with accurate resource paths and host information.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Corrected authentication redirects when using configured or forwarded host details.\n  * Added clear errors for unsupported discovery paths.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Clarified that `BASE_URL` must be an HTTP(S) origin without paths, credentials, queries, or fragments.\n  * Updated proxy configuration examples to include the URL scheme.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n",
